                     "standfirst":  "A double bill for a hundred years of community cinema: the Cinema For All documentary Rebels with Projectors, then Tornatore's Cinema Paradiso. Tickets were three pounds.",
                     "story":  [
                                   "We joined the Festival of Community Cinema, a nationwide celebration of a hundred years of volunteer-led cinema in Britain and of the programming that has come out of it.",
                                   "The night opened with <em>Rebels with Projectors</em>, a new documentary produced by Cinema For All about the people who have kept community cinema running for a century. Then Tornatore's Oscar-winning <em>Cinema Paradiso</em>, which is a film about exactly that: a village hall, a projectionist, and a whole town growing up in front of the same screen.",
                                   "We took it to the Genesis in Whitechapel, an independent cinema with well over a century of history on the Mile End Road. Tickets were three pounds, because a hundred years of community cinema is not something to price people out of."
